---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Documentation">
<main class="min-h-screen max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16 lg:px-10 lg:py-20">
<header class="max-w-3xl border-b border-neutral-900 pb-10">
<p class="lab-label mb-4">Reference / Lab</p>
<h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">Documentation</h1>
<p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-neutral-400">How the Engineering Lab is structured, maintained and evolved.</p>
</header>
<article class="prose prose-invert mt-12 max-w-3xl">
<h2>What the Lab is</h2>
<p>Alok Engineering Lab is a long-term engineering archive rather than a conventional portfolio. Projects record substantial systems. Writing develops technical ideas. Notes preserve durable knowledge. Experiments capture questions and evidence. Timeline records the journey.</p>
<h2>Content model</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Projects</strong> — substantial engineering systems and case studies.</li>
<li><strong>Writing</strong> — developed technical explanations and arguments.</li>
<li><strong>Notes</strong> — compact ideas, principles and observations.</li>
<li><strong>Experiments</strong> — bounded questions, setups, observations and results.</li>
<li><strong>Timeline</strong> — important engineering milestones and turning points.</li>
<li><strong>Changelog</strong> — meaningful releases and product checkpoints.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Engineering principles</h2>
<p>Inspect before modifying. Prefer simple systems. Make decisions explicit. Test reality rather than intention. Keep authority boundaries clear. Treat failures as information. Preserve provenance where trust matters.</p>
<h2>Technology</h2>
<p>The site uses Astro, Tailwind CSS, TypeScript and content collections, deployed as a static site. The architecture intentionally avoids a database, CMS and paid services.</p>
<h2>Maintenance</h2>
<p><a href="/docs/content-workflow/">The content workflow</a> documents the Git-native publishing contract, validation gates and repository-native content scaffolding.</p>
<p><a href="/explore/">Explore the full archive</a> searches published records across the Lab, while <a href="/connections/">Connections</a> exposes the repository-backed knowledge graph.</p>
<p>The preferred workflow is <strong>inspect → implement → verify → review → checkpoint</strong>. Current repository state and Git history are stronger sources of truth than old conversations.</p>
</article>
</main>
</Layout>
